"1380" height="63" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="_view_contract" value="Question: How does the complete request travel through the relevant trust boundaries while preserving authorization and tenant scope? How does the complete request travel through the relevant trust boundaries while preserving authorization and&lt;br&gt;tenant scope? How does the complete request travel through the relevant trust boundaries while preserving authorization and tenant scope?&lt;br&gt;Decision: Choose the smallest bounded request flow, retaining independent evidence and explicit uncertainty on every unsupported relationship. Choose the smallest bounded request flow, retaining independent evidence and explicit uncertainty on&lt;br&gt;every unsupported relationship. Choose the smallest bounded request flow, retaining independent evidence and explicit uncertainty on every unsupported relationship.&lt;br&gt;Scenario: A tenant issues one request, receives a deterministic ordered page, and examines related records without an unbounded per-record fan-out. A tenant issues one request, receives a deterministic ordered page, and examines related records&lt;br&gt;without an unbounded per-record fan-out. A tenant issues one request, receives a deterministic ordered page, and examines related records without an unbounded per-record fan-out.&lt;br&gt;Invariant: Keep parent pagination, empty relations, authorization boundaries, relationship direction and complete citation metadata unchanged. Keep parent pagination, empty relations, authorization boundaries, relationship direction and complete&lt;br&gt;citation metadata unchanged. Keep parent pagination, empty relations, authorization boundaries, relationship direction and complete citation metadata unchanged.&lt;br&gt;Status: proposed&lt;br&gt;View evidence: docs/example-architecture.md:20&lt;br&gt;Omissions: Production capacity is not established by this synthetic presentation exercise. Production capacity is not established by this synthetic presentation exercise. Production capacity is not established by this synthetic presentation&lt;br&gt;exercise. , No remote resources or citation targets are fetched during rendering. No remote resources or citation targets are fetched during rendering. No remote resources or citation targets are fetched during rendering." style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;fontColor=#616E7C;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="189" width="1380" height="176" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="_rule" value="" style="line;html=1;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#1E6FD9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="373" width="120" height="10" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="_group_ingress" value="Managed Edge &amp;amp; Public Ingress Boundary — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility " style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;fontColor=#616E7C;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10" y="444" width="240" height="339" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="_group_core" value="Internal Payment Core &amp;amp; Processing Subsystem — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility  — explicit security boundary and ownership responsibility " style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;fontColor=#616E7C;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="715" wid